FAQFIX={
("bpc-157","What is the BPC-157 dosage?"):"There's no established human dose because it's research-only. Studies have mostly been in animals, using a range of routes.",
("bpc-157","Is BPC-157 FDA-approved?"):"No. It's sold for research purposes only. WADA lists it as prohibited in sport.",
("bpc-157","Does BPC-157 work in humans?"):"It hasn't been tested in controlled human trials. A 2026 review found 3 small, uncontrolled studies with 30 people in total; most reported improvement, but the authors rated the certainty of evidence very low.",
("bpc-157","Is BPC-157 safe?"):"There's no clinical safety data in humans yet (<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40756949/\" rel=\"noopener\">Vasireddi et al., HSS Journal 2025</a>). Animal studies reported no harmful effects, but unregulated products can be contaminated or mislabeled.",
("bpc-157","Why do BPC-157 doses online differ so much?"):"Most numbers come from animal studies, which used different amounts and routes.",
("tb-500","What is the TB-500 dosage?"):"There's no established human dose because it's research-only.",
("tb-500","Does TB-500 work?"):"Research on thymosin beta-4, the parent protein, shows repair activity, including a benefit in early-dosed heart-attack patients. Controlled trials of TB-500 itself haven't been published yet.",
("ghk-cu","Does GHK-Cu reverse aging?"):"Lab and gene-expression studies link it to skin repair and collagen production. Large human anti-aging trials haven't been done yet.",
("collagen-peptides","Do collagen peptides work for skin?"):"Yes, in trials. Meta-analyses (26 trials, 1,721 people in one) found improved skin hydration and elasticity compared with placebo.",
("retatrutide","Can I buy real retatrutide?"):"Lilly's retatrutide is only available in clinical trials right now. Products sold online are labeled for research purposes only.",
("retatrutide","Is retatrutide stronger than tirzepatide?"):"Its average trial results are bigger, up to −25.0% vs tirzepatide's −20.2% in SURMOUNT-5, though there's no head-to-head trial yet.",
("cjc-1295-ipamorelin","What is the CJC-1295 ipamorelin dosage?"):"There's no established human dose because both are research-only.",
("cjc-1295-ipamorelin","Is CJC-1295 FDA-approved?"):"No. It's sold for research purposes only.",
("cjc-1295-ipamorelin","Does ipamorelin work?"):"It triggers growth-hormone release and was well tolerated in a 114-patient hospital trial, though that trial didn't speed gut recovery after surgery.",
("mots-c","What is the MOTS-c dosage?"):"There's no established human dose because it's research-only. Human trials are just starting.",
("mots-c","Does MOTS-c work like exercise?"):"In mice it improved how the body handles sugar and fat (<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25738459/\" rel=\"noopener\">Cell Metab 2015</a>), which is where the nickname comes from. Human trials will show how much carries over.",
("semax","What is the Semax dosage?"):"There's no FDA-established human dose. The main human study used it in stroke rehab.",
("semax","Does Semax improve focus?"):"It raised BDNF, a brain growth factor, in stroke patients. Trials in healthy people haven't been done yet.",
}
